Prefix: : <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/security-identity-boundaries#>
Prefix: xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

Ontology: <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/security-identity-boundaries>


# ************************************************************************
# Security Identity Boundaries
# ************************************************************************
#
# Models the distinction between a Security and the identifiers, identifier
# assignments, system records and market listings that refer to or represent
# it. The example focuses on identity boundaries rather than lifecycle.
#

Datatype: xsd:date
Datatype: xsd:decimal
Datatype: xsd:string

### Financial things

Class: FinancialThing

Class: Security
    SubClassOf: FinancialThing

Class: Listing
    SubClassOf: FinancialThing

Class: TradingVenue
    SubClassOf: FinancialThing


### Identifiers and identification schemes

Class: Identifier

Class: IdentifierScheme

DataProperty: identifierValue
    Domain: Identifier
    Range: xsd:string

ObjectProperty: governedByScheme
    Domain: Identifier
    Range: IdentifierScheme

ObjectProperty: identifiedBy
    Domain: Security
    Range: Identifier


### Identifier assignment

# A direct Security-to-Identifier relationship may be enough for a simple
# ontology. IdentifierAssignment becomes useful when the assignment itself
# needs authority, scope, temporal context or provenance.

Class: IdentifierAssignment

Class: AssignmentAuthority

Class: TemporalContext

ObjectProperty: hasIdentifierAssignment
    Domain: Security
    Range: IdentifierAssignment

ObjectProperty: identifies
    Domain: IdentifierAssignment
    Range: Security

ObjectProperty: usesIdentifier
    Domain: IdentifierAssignment
    Range: Identifier

ObjectProperty: underScheme
    Domain: IdentifierAssignment
    Range: IdentifierScheme

ObjectProperty: assignedBy
    Domain: IdentifierAssignment
    Range: AssignmentAuthority

ObjectProperty: hasTemporalContext
    Domain: IdentifierAssignment
    Range: TemporalContext


### Core identifier-assignment semantics

Class: SecurityIdentifierAssignment
    SubClassOf:
        IdentifierAssignment,
        identifies exactly 1 Security,
        usesIdentifier exactly 1 Identifier,
        underScheme exactly 1 IdentifierScheme


### System records

Class: SystemRecord

ObjectProperty: represents
    Domain: SystemRecord
    Range: FinancialThing


### Security listings

ObjectProperty: hasListing
    Domain: Security
    Range: Listing

ObjectProperty: admittedTo
    Domain: Listing
    Range: TradingVenue

DataProperty: tickerSymbol
    Domain: Listing
    Range: xsd:string


### Identity boundaries expressed by the model

# Security, Identifier, IdentifierAssignment, SystemRecord and Listing are
# modelled as distinct concepts because they answer different questions:
#
# Security             - What is the financial thing?
# Identifier           - What value identifies or refers to it?
# IdentifierAssignment - In what assignment context is an identifier used?
# SystemRecord         - What information-system artefact represents it?
# Listing              - What market-specific presence does it have?
#
# No broad DisjointClasses axiom is added here. The important modelling
# lesson is the distinction in meaning, not a blanket logical separation
# between every category in every possible ontology.
